NNAAMMEE
     aauuttooiinnssttaallll — unattended OpenBSD installation and upgrade

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     aauuttooiinnssttaallll allows unattended installation or upgrade of OpenBSD by auto‐
     matically responding to installer questions with answers from a response
     file.  aauuttooiinnssttaallll uses DHCP to discover the location of the response
     file and HTTP to fetch the file.  If that fails, the installer asks for
     the location which can either be a URL or a local path.

     See install.site(5) for how to provide custom configuration.

     To start unattended installation or upgrade choose '(A)utoinstall' at the
     install prompt.  If there is only one network interface, the installer
     fetches the response file via that interface.  If there is more than one
     network interface, a selection is presented and the installer fetches the
     response file via the selected interface.

     If the machine is netbooted, the aauuttooiinnssttaallll feature is invoked if the
     user does not intervene within a short time.  It behaves as if the user
     selected '(A)utoinstall', but always fetches the response file via the
     netboot interface.

